    "background_story": "Ryder was a laid-back surfer who lived life on his own terms. When faced with problems, he'd often respond with a casual shrug, as if to say, 'whatever, dude.' His carefree attitude was both captivating and infuriating to those around him. Despite his nonchalant demeanor, Ryder had a hidden talent for art. His paintings were a reflection of his easygoing nature, with bold brushstrokes and vibrant colors. One day, a local gallery owner stumbled upon Ryder's work and offered him a solo exhibition. Ryder's response? A characteristic shrug, followed by a smile and a 'sure, why not?' The show became a huge success, with critics praising Ryder's unique style. He remained unphased by the attention, continuing to create art on his own terms, with a shrug and a smile.",
